nodecode-pocket is a rewrite of Belweave's Belweave/hermes-notify:
https://github.com/Belweave/hermes-notify
commit 698b66b6d64a87d317ba97938f37f9ed75f04cd6
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Preetham Kyanam (LICENSE)

Rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract: the three Notify
Agent API writes a release or a task actually needs — an update for the
phone (POST /notifications), a question with its decision or written answer
(POST /interactions, then GET /interactions/{id}[/wait]), and the same read
again by id (GET /interactions/{id}) — with the same fixed origin, bearer
key, idempotency key and one-wait ceiling of 25 seconds, as three tools
(notify_send, notify_ask, notify_poll), a /pocket command and the manual on
(help :pocket). The tool schemas are contract declarations, so a tool
cannot advertise one shape and read another, and the whole HTTP seam is one
function a test binds.

Left out, because Nodecode already answers them or they need Hermes's own
runtime: the release workspace with measured stages and checks
(notify_release), publishing the workspace to the operator's Cloudflare
Worker (notify_publish_app), the six tools' sqlite journal and idempotency
ledger (this cell keeps the last eight receipts in memory instead), the
native Hermes approval transport that intercepts a command before it runs
(Nodecode's tools ask the question inside a tool call; the person's answer
arrives as that call's answer), automatic progress updates and Live
Activities, the bundled skill, the web/desktop App, and the signed webhook
receipt.
